{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Send screen-opened and state-transition events to any analytics backend with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every screen that models its state with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" already knows exactly when it was opened and when it moves between Empty, Loading, Data, and Error. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" turns those moments into ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"s and fans them out to as many ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"s as you register — one per analytics backend (Firebase, Mixpanel, Amplitude, your own logging endpoint, a debug console print, …)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates ships no backend-specific tracker implementations, so the core module stays dependency-free — but it does include ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (logs every event to the console) and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (silently discards everything), so you don’t have to hand-roll a console logger just to confirm events fire at the right moments. For a real backend, write one small adapter, converting the event’s backend-agnostic "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue"},{"text":" parameters into that SDK’s own format:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct FirebaseScreenTracker: ScreenAnalyticsTracker {","    func track(_ event: ScreenAnalyticsEvent) {","        Analytics.logEvent(event.name, parameters: event.parameters.mapValues { value in","            switch value {","            case .string(let string): string","            case .int(let int): int","            case .double(let double): double","            case .bool(let bool): bool","            }","        })","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An adapter is also free to remap ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event.name"},{"type":"text","text":" to whatever vocabulary its backend expects — Firebase, for example, reserves a specific constant for screen views."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Wiring a screen","anchor":"Wiring-a-screen","type":"heading","level":2},{"code":["let analytics = ScreenAnalyticsService(trackers: [FirebaseScreenTracker(), PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker()])","","func onAppear(source: ScreenOpenSource<AppScreen>) {","    analytics.trackScreenOpened(\"Articles\", source: source.analyticsKind)","    analytics.observeStateChanges(of: store, screen: \"Articles\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreenOpened(_:source:)"},{"text":" sends one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_opened"},{"type":"text","text":" event. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withObservationTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" mechanism "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" uses to mirror a store, and sends a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"type":"text","text":" event for every subsequent "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" transition — call it once, right where you create or first observe the store. When a transition lands on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", the event also carries the error’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It also times how long the screen spends in ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the moment the state leaves "},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it sends a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_load_duration"},{"text":" event (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenLoadDuration(screen:outcome:milliseconds:)","isActive":true},{"text":") with that outcome and the elapsed time in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration_ms"},{"text":" — useful for a “how long do loads actually take, and how often do they end in an error” dashboard without hand-rolling a stopwatch around every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"text":" call.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"text":" event landing on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":" tells you a screen failed to load; it doesn’t tell you whether the user gave up or hit Retry. Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenRetryTapped(screen:)","isActive":true},{"text":") from the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"text":" closure you pass to the Error placeholder, so that’s a distinct, countable event instead of indistinguishable from the screen’s initial ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["ScreenStateView(store.state, onRetry: {","    analytics.trackRetryTapped(\"Articles\")","    Task { await store.load { try await api.fetchArticles() } }","}) { articles in","    ArticleList(articles)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadNextPage(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t move "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" off "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" on either a success or a failure, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":" has nothing to report for it — call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackNextPageLoaded(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackNextPageFailed(_:errorDescription:)"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageLoaded(screen:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageFailed(screen:errorDescription:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") from the same place you call "},{"code":"loadNextPage(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring how "},{"code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func loadMore() async {","    await store.loadNextPage { try await api.fetchArticles(page: nextPage) }","    if let error = store.loadNextPageError {","        analytics.trackNextPageFailed(\"Articles\", errorDescription: error.localizedDescription)","    } else {","        analytics.trackNextPageLoaded(\"Articles\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" expose an ","type":"text"},{"code":"analyticsKind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" helper — a short, stable, payload-free name for the current case (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"loading\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"error\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"push\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"deep_link\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …) — so you can build custom ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"s yourself for anything the built-in factories don’t cover.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/TrackingAnalytics","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Analytics","title":"Analytics"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/trackinganalytics"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Tracking Screen Analytics","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenAnalyticsEvent/screenRetryTapped(screen:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"The default event for a user tapping Retry on an Error placeholder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— distinct from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenOpened(screen:source:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", so analytics can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tell “user hit retry” apart from the screen’s initial open. Call it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure passed to the Error placeholder;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStates has no way to detect a retry tap on its own, since the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default placeholders know nothing about analytics.","type":"text"}],"title":"screenRetryTapped(screen:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenRetryTapped(screen:)","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenanalyticsevent\/screenretrytapped(screen:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"screenRetryTapped"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"screen"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScreenAnalyticsEvent","preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A14AnalyticsEventV"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenAnalyticsEvent/screenOpened(screen:source:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenanalyticsevent\/screenopened(screen:source:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenOpened(screen:source:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"screenOpened","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"screen","kind":"external